<https://id.i2idl.org/definitions/assessment-literacy> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "ERIC scope note: Knowledge of the key principles, methods, standards, and other aspects of assessment; and the ability to use that knowledge to design, plan, and conduct tests and use their results to improve teaching and learning." <https://id.i2idl.org/graphs/concepts/assessment-literacy/versions/1> .
<https://id.i2idl.org/definitions/assessment-literacy> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://glossarystudio.app/ns/Definition> <https://id.i2idl.org/graphs/concepts/assessment-literacy/versions/1> .
<https://id.i2idl.org/definitions/assessment-literacy> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value> "The knowledge and skills needed to design, select, interpret, and use assessments and their results appropriately in educational practice." <https://id.i2idl.org/graphs/concepts/assessment-literacy/versions/1> .
